NG, Goal 2): '.prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-critic-trim.md:10 \u2014 data-model carries 8 `## Direction` norm(s) but this plan disposes of 7'. The missing one is the governance-document lifecycle norm ('A governance document reaches a terminal state; it is never deleted...'). Scope: instance. Add a disposition for it to the plan's governed_by data-model entry (likely 'inapplicable because no plan is archived or deleted by this change').", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-critic-trim.md"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "record_lint_partial silently merges distinct record-lint results that share a check and location", "recommendation": "Scope: class. Why it broke: record_lint_partial names each entry `record-lint <check>: <where>` (where = path[:line], or the literal 'unchecked'), and merge_findings/merge_observations dedupe on (goal, name, files), so any two results of one check at the same path with no or the same line collapse into one and the others' detail is dropped. Real members: several missing deliverables declared on one `**Deliverables:**` line (buildplan_refs assigns one line_num per line, so they share `chunk 01:<line>`); several problems in one change fragment (change-fragment is emitted with line None per problem); several unreasoned budgets (learnings-budget-unreasoned is always project-state.yaml with line None); two chunks' `chunk-ref-missing unchecked` entries (all named `...: unchecked`). The gate still blocks on the survivor, but the builder sees one missing deliverable, fixes it, and buys another round to learn of the next \u2014 the reviewer relay this replaces listed each. Fix through the one owner: put a discriminator in the record-lint entry's identity (e.g. include the detail, or an index, in the name/key built in record_lint_partial) and add a test feeding two same-check same-location results and asserting both reach the fact. No current test covers duplicate results.", "files": ["plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py", "tests/test_critic_consolidate.py"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "severity": "warning", "title": "Consolidation re-files record-lint results the builder already accepted, bypassing prior_dispositions", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. Before this change a record-lint result reached the fact only through a reviewer, and every reviewer was told 'Do not re-raise one absent material change' via the manifest's prior_dispositions. record_lint_partial now appends every result to every review fact unconditionally, with a fresh fid, and nothing in build_fact_body consults prior_dispositions. So a governed-by-gap or other WARNING accepted with `disposition --accept` is re-asked on every subsequent cumulative/verify review, and a BLOCKING result accepted with --owner-ruling (e.g. a chunk-ref-missing false positive) re-blocks unresolved_blocking on each new fact and needs a fresh owner ruling every round \u2014 the exact round-buying the prior_dispositions contract exists to prevent, and it contradicts the plan's 'review wall-clock is P0 -> conforms' disposition. Either filter (or demote to an observation) results matching a prior disposition on (title, files) in record_lint_partial, with a test, or record the decision that machine results always re-file and say so in the reviewer-facing prior_dispositions text.", "files": ["plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "warning", "title": "Governing-Artifact Reconciliation still tells a reviewer to raise the governed-by-gap WARNING that consolidation now records itself, and no coordinator role is assigned to run it", "recommendation": "Scope: class. It broke because this change gave one check two producers: record_lint's `governed-by-gap` (record_lint.SEVERITY = warning, now recorded into the fact by `record_lint_partial`), and cross-checks.md 'Governing-Artifact Reconciliation', whose middle arm still says 'A governing norm with no disposition line ... -> WARNING (Goal 2)'. That is the same paperwork gap. The same file tells reviewers to 'Never raise, restate, re-derive or recount' a record-lint result ('your copy would be a second finding about the same record'), so the file now contradicts itself. Under the old protocol the Goal 2 holder relayed the lint result and could merge the two into one finding. Now the machine's finding is named 'record-lint governed-by-gap: <path>:<line>' and a reviewer's finding gets a free-form name. `merge_findings` dedups on (goal, name, files), so the two never merge, and the builder pays for two dispositions of one gap. This review shows it: the manifest's record_lint carries a governed-by-gap on build-plan-critic-trim.md:10. The section also has no owner under a coordinator roster. coordinator.md and agents/critic-reviewer.md give sustainability 'Goals 5, 6 + the Records Pass' only, and review-protocol.md files it under '## Framework-Specific Checks', which the design role runs only when framework files change. Fix in one place: delete the WARNING arm from Governing-Artifact Reconciliation and point at record-lint as its single producer. Keep only what the lint cannot see: the BLOCKING departure (owned by Goal 3), and the 'no governed_by: at all' observation if record-lint does not emit it. Then name that remainder in exactly one role's brief, or fold it into Goal 3 and Goal 2 text and drop the subsection.", "files": ["plugin/skills/critic/cross-checks.md", "plugin/skills/critic/coordinator.md", "plugin/agents/critic-reviewer.md", "plugin/skills/critic/review-protocol.md"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "Comments still describe the deleted Stop-hook learnings cross-check note, and the PR protocol still counts three backlog-cache surfaces", "recommendation": "Scope: class. These are claims about consumers this change removed, and the sweep searched for the removed checks' names rather than for what was said about their consumers. Sites found: (1) plugin/bin/prawduct-hook `cmd_learnings_files` docstring, 'The Stop hook's cross-check note reads the session span directly (`learnings_change_set`)'. That note (`gates.learnings_cross_check_note`) is deleted. (2) The inline comment in the same function, '`learnings_change_set` is also what the Stop-hook cross-check note reads, so the two can no longer disagree'. (3) The `gates.learnings_change_set` docstring, which justifies one definition shared by 'both readers' (the gate nudge and the reviewer). Its only caller is now the fallback in `learnings_review_change_set`. (4) plugin/skills/pr/review-protocol.md R-1 text, 'the one home all three review surfaces route to'. cache-reads.md now says two. The fix is to delete each claim, not reword it. To find more, search for the deleted nudge and for counts of cache-reads consumers. Prose ceiling: nothing reads these lines. The keep-or-retire question for `learnings-files --for-diff` is already recorded in the plan as an owner decision, so this note does not raise it again.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/lib/gates.py", "plugin/skills/pr/review-protocol.md"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "Docstring and comment overclaim that a boundary observations array 'cannot launder a severity'", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. The `validate_partial` docstring says 'It cannot launder a severity: a blocking entry is refused there, and at the boundary a WARNING is a finding by the protocol's own table'. The comment that replaced the boundary refusal in `consolidate` says much the same. Only the first half is enforced in code. A cumulative reviewer who puts a WARNING in `observations` consolidates with no trace, because the 'protocol's table' is prose, and that path is exactly what the deleted refusal was written to close. The owner accepted this tradeoff, and WARNINGs gate nothing, so the impact is limited to dispositions