 "fid": "R-7"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "warning", "title": "scope-trace: the removal orphaned producers whose only consumer was the retired passes", "recommendation": "Scope: class. Why it broke: the change removed consumers (the Learnings Cross-Check, Backlog Reconciliation and the Stop nudge's learnings_cross_check_note) without sweeping the producers they were the only readers of. Members found by grep over plugin/: `prawduct-hook learnings-files --for-diff` and gates.learnings_review_change_set, plus learnings_change_set, which is now reached only as that function's fallback. No skill, agent, methodology or hook names --for-diff any more. Also `backlog cache-query affecting` and `created-since`: after this change cache-reads.md lists only the PR reviewer and the janitor as consumers, and neither uses those two ops (the janitor uses by-area). Yet cache-reads.md still documents both ops as part of 'the contract shared by the review-time readers'. The plan records only the first as 'Not settled by the goals \u2014 left for the owner' and does not mention the cache ops. Consequence: the code and grants for these verbs stay maintained and tested with nothing reaching them. That is the 'channel produced and never consumed' that core.md calls a defect ('A channel that is produced and never consumed is a DEFECT'). Bound the class by asking, for each removed pass, what it called. The owner should rule once on the whole set (delete, or name a consumer), not on --for-diff alone.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/lib/gates.py", "plugin/skills/backlog/cache-reads.md"], "fid": "R-8"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "warning", "title": "The plan's 'PR reviewer is untouched' constraint was departed from with no recorded mid-build decision", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. Why it broke: Chunk 03 edited plugin/skills/pr/review-protocol.md (the R-1 rationale and the Learnings Cross-Check section) to stop falsely naming the Critic as the owner of those scans. The correction is legitimate ('A chunk boundary defers a DELETION, never a CORRECTION'). But the plan's Constraints still say 'The PR reviewer is untouched (#1129)', and 'Decisions made mid-build' does not record the departure. Consequence: the owner exercising the boundary veto, and whoever builds #1129 from this plan, will read that the PR protocol is unchanged when its stated rationale for not walking the backlog or learnings has been rewritten. Fix: add a mid-build decision line saying what changed in the PR protocol and that its behaviour (incidental-only R-1, no learnings scan) is unchanged. The plan is a free surface.", "files": ["plugin/skills/pr/review-protocol.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-critic-trim.md"], "fid": "R-9"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "warning", "title": "A plan inference falsified mid-build is still marked Inferred, and two owner rulings are open at the boundary", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. The Goals section still carries '*Inferred:* the mid-build decisions list is printed by critic-consolidate from the plan's Goals section'. The Chunk 02 decision shows this is false: nothing prints it, because no reader exists. Two mid-build decisions are marked 'Not settled by the goals': (1) dropping the mid-build decisions NOTE with no replacement, and (2) keeping learnings-files --for-diff without a consumer. Consequence: this is the boundary at which the plan asked the owner to veto inferences, and the record presents a falsified inference as a live one. Fix: strike or resolve the inference, and get the owner's ruling on both items before merge. Record each ruling somewhere other than this plan, since a governance change cannot be its own only witness.", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-critic-trim.md"], "fid": "R-10"}, {"goal": "Learnings Cross-Check", "severity": "warning", "title": "Learnings Cross-Check: the Chunk 03 sweep edited tokens, not claims, and left descriptions of the retired passes live", "recommendation": "Scope: class. Escalated from prose NOTE because the change reintroduces the pattern core.md warns against: 'A mechanism change is done when every artifact DESCRIBING it agrees: search for the claim, not the tokens you edited'. hook-surface.md also applies: 'A docstring or comment is a claim... after a reversal... re-grep your own prose for the old world'. The plan's own Chunk 03 acceptance criterion is that the falsifying greps return only history. Survivors found by grepping the concept: (a) the prawduct-hook learnings-files docstring ('The Stop hook's cross-check note reads the session span directly') and its inline comment ('learnings_change_set is also what the Stop-hook cross-check note reads, so the two can no longer disagree'). That note was deleted in this change. (b) gates.learnings_change_set's docstring ('That is the span both readers mean \u2014 the gate is judging this session, and the reviewer...') and learnings_review_change_set's ('the Stop nudge and the reviewer must never give different answers'). Both readers are gone. The tell is that the diff changed 'both callers' to 'every caller' in that same docstring while one caller remains. (c) plugin/skills/pr/review-protocol.md R-1 resolver bullet: 'the one home all three review surfaces route to'; cache-reads.md now names two. (d) documentation/backlog-service-requirements.md GV10 still names 'the Critic Backlog Reconciliation' as a backstop, and documentation/backlog-service-cache-spec.md lists it and C-B1\u2013C-B4 as consumers 1\u20134. Remedy: delete or make relational each claim. The construction that would have enumerated them is a `Retires:` declaration ('Learnings Cross-Check', 'Backlog Reconciliation', 'cross-check note') on a Direction entry or project-state decision, so that retired-claim-survives finds the survivors. Search over the whole repo (documentation/ included), not just plugin/.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/lib/gates.py", "plugin/skills/pr/review-protocol.md"], "fid": "R-11"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Mid-build decisions for the owner (critic-trim)", "recommendation": "Scope: none. (1) Ch.02 mid-build decisions NOTE removed with no replacement: NOT settled by the goals, and an alignment-pass miss (the Goals' first inference assumed a reader of `## Goals` that does not exist). (2) Ch.02 record-lint ratings moved into record_lint.SEVERITY / INNER_BLOCKING / _UNCHECKED_SHAPES, with stage narrowing in consolidation: settled by 'Record-lint results reach the builder from the code that computes them'. (3) Ch.02 the `none` scope answer retired with the mandated cross-checks: settled by the same goal. (4) Ch.03 Stop nudge stops naming a learnings read list, and learnings-files --for-diff is kept without a consumer: NOT settled by the goals, left for the owner. Unrecorded: the PR protocol edits against the 'PR reviewer is untouched' constraint (see the separate finding).", "fid": "R-12"}, {"goal": "Backlog Reconciliation", "severity": "note", "title": "Backlog item appears resolved: brookstalley/prawduct#1128 'critic: reviewers stop relaying machine checks and null notes'", "recommendation": "Scope: none. The change fragment declares `closes: [brookstalley/prawduct#1128]`, and the cache shows it open. Verify it, then call `/prawduct:backlog update 1128 status=shipped closed-by=scope:critic-trim` when the backlog skill's 'When to mark shipped' rule says to (at the release that ships it, under gitflow). Cited #1129, #1130 and #641 all resolve and are open (no C-B4 dangling ids).", "fid": "R-13"}, {"goal": "Backlog Reconciliation", "severity": "note", "title": "C-B3: open critic-area items touched by this change, none updated", "recommendation": "Scope: none. `affecting` on the changed critic files returns #641 ('deleting a mechanism leaves stale assertions undetected'), #672 and #928. #641 is directly exercised by this change's surv